# Day 2 Notes
- concat stacks data (same columns) to add more rows; ignore_index=True gives a fresh 0..n-1 index.
- pd.merge(               # call Pandas merge function to join two DataFrames
    df1,         # left DataFrame (keep all rows from this one)
    df2,          # right DataFrame (bring matching columns from this one)
    on="col_name",   # column used as the matching key in both tables
    how="left"          # left join: keep all rows from orders_all, fill missing matches with NaN

